AniPals – Vibe Coding Additional Rules and Way-of-working

Development Philosophy

The development process of AniPals focuses on clean collaboration, readable code, stable feature implementation, and consistent progress tracking. Team members are encouraged to prioritize maintainability and communication throughout the project lifecycle.


Team Collaboration Rules

Task Assignment
- Each member is assigned specific responsibilities and features.
- Members should avoid modifying another member’s code without permission.
- Major feature changes must first be discussed with the team.

Communication
- Team updates should be shared regularly.
- Bugs, blockers, and unfinished tasks must be reported immediately.
- Important development decisions should be documented.

Contribution Expectations
- Every member should commit meaningful progress regularly.
- Inactive or unfinished tasks should be communicated early.
- Members should assist each other when integration issues occur.


GitHub and Version Control Workflow

Branching Workflow
- Main branch contains stable code only.
- Feature development should preferably use separate branches.
- Merge changes only after testing.

Commit Rules
- Commit messages must clearly describe the update.
- Avoid vague commit messages such as:
  - update
  - fix
  - changes

Example Good Commit Messages
- Added gacha pity system
- Created login API endpoint
- Fixed multiplayer trade confirmation bug

Push Rules
- Push code regularly to avoid data loss.
- Pull latest repository changes before starting development.


Coding Standards

Code Readability
- Use meaningful variable and function names.
- Keep functions modular and organized.
- Avoid unnecessary duplication of code.

File Organization
- Separate frontend and backend logic properly.
- Store reusable components in organized folders.
- Maintain consistent naming conventions.

Documentation
- Complex systems should include comments or explanations.
- API endpoints should be documented when added.


Testing and Quality Assurance

Testing Rules
- Features must be tested before pushing.
- Bugs discovered during testing should be fixed immediately.
- Multiplayer features must be checked for synchronization issues.

Gameplay Validation
The following systems must be verified carefully:
- Gacha pity calculations
- Weather event activation
- Trading confirmations
- Inventory synchronization
- Offline progression rewards


Development Priorities

Priority Order
1. User authentication system
2. Database integration
3. Core farming gameplay
4. Gacha system
5. Weather event system
6. Multiplayer interactions
7. UI improvements and polish


UI/UX Development Rules

Interface Design
- Maintain a cozy and colorful pixel-art atmosphere.
- Keep menus simple and readable.
- Avoid overcrowding the interface.

User Experience
- Tutorials should guide first-time players clearly.
- Important player actions should display confirmation prompts.
- Animations and transitions should remain smooth and responsive.


Final Development Rules
- Prioritize stability over unnecessary features.
- Keep gameplay systems balanced and fair.
- Maintain respectful teamwork and collaboration.
- Ensure all project files are backed up through GitHub regularly.
